In `boxplot_stats`, for each dataset `x`, the code computes `q1, med, q3 = np.percentile(x, [25, 50, 75])` and then immediately sets `stats['iqr'] = q3 - q1`. Since `q1` and `q3` are the 25th and 75th percentiles of the same array, they are ordered by percentile level, so `q1 <= q3`. The test suite only feeds non-empty single datasets into this function, and there is no later reassignment of `q1` or `q3` before the `iqr` computation, so the property holds at every evaluation.

